From 52f2c4c05d2c7baed9e0e8765c21c7db7dc5cbb9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Rao <jack.rao@baseten.co>
Date: Fri, 7 Aug 2026 01:32:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf(server): run the GLM fp32 LM-head GEMM on tensor cores
 via scoped TF32 (LPS-1062)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Both operands of the fp32 base head projection are exact bf16 upcasts, so
TF32 multiplies them exactly and accumulates in fp32 — numerically equivalent
to the FP32 SIMT kernel modulo summation order, but on tensor cores instead
of CUDA cores (~115 ms -> ~few ms per 4096-token chunk on B300). Scoped to a
custom autograd.Function (fwd + dgrad; base weight frozen under LoRA), gated
on TP1/no-bias/frozen-weight/CUDA, kill-switch BT_TF32_FP32_HEAD=0.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
